.TH "CRUFT" "1" "September 2026" "cruft" "cruft User Manual"
.SH NAME
.PP
cruft \- Calculinux reduced footprint framebuffer terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.B cruft
.RB [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B cruft
is a Linux framebuffer terminal emulator derived from yaft, tuned for
low memory on Calculinux devices.
.PP
When a status font is installed, cruft draws a status bar in the margin
strip above the cell grid: a wifi signal stair on the left, the clock
in the centre, and a backlight meter and battery indicator on the
right. A segment whose data source is absent (bare hardware, VM) is
hidden; a missing or unsuitable status font disables the bar entirely
and the grid reclaims the full screen.
.PP
Images are shown through two protocols that land on the same sparse
per-cell pixmaps: sixel (device control sequence 62 t) and the kitty
graphics protocol (OSC 1337). The kitty path accepts \fIFile ;\fP
transfers of raw BGR/BGRA pixels (dimensions required) and of PNG
images, when the binary was built against the system libpng (detected
automatically; force the decision with
.B HAVE_PNG=0
or
.BR HAVE_PNG=1 ).
Decoded images are capped at 512x512 pixels, anchored at the cursor,
shrunk (aspect-preserving) to fit the remaining grid, and never scroll
the screen. \fIImage ;\fP operators (query, delete, chunked upload, ...)
are not implemented but are always answered with an
.I ok=false
\fIRep\fP reply, so clients that probe for them degrade instead of
hanging.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.PP
Rewrite conf.h before make.
The default status bar segment selection (used when
.B CRUFT_SB
is unset) is the
.B sb_default_segments
conf.h variable (default "all").
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B FRAMEBUFFER
Specify framebuffer device (default /dev/fb0).
.TP
.B CRUFT_FONT
Path to a CRUFTFN1 font blob (default /usr/share/cruft/console.cruftfont).
.TP
.B CRUFT
If this variable includes "wall", cruft enables wallpaper mode and a
framebuffer shadow buffer. See cruft_wall.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB
Status bar segments: a comma-separated list of
.B time ,
.B wifi ,
.B battery
and/or
.BR brightness ,
or
.B all
(the default) to show every segment whose source is present,
.B none
(or
.BR 0 )
to disable the bar. Unknown names are ignored with a warning.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB_12H
Set to 1 for a 12-hour clock (\fIH:MMam/pm\fP); the default is
24-hour.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB_FONT
Path to the 4x8 CRUFTFN1 status font
(default /usr/share/cruft/status.cruftfont, installed by the
miniwi-console package).
